VeridianOS: kwrited's KDED module in its own source file

kwrited is built either as an executable (without libutempter, as here)
or as a KDED module. kwrited.cpp held both, the module part and its
"#include "kwrited.moc"" under #if !BUILD_AS_EXECUTABLE. AutoMoc does not
evaluate #if, so the executable build ran moc for kwrited.cpp as well,
which (with the module compiled out) found nothing: "kwrited.cpp: note:
No relevant classes found. No output generated."

The module's constructor, destructor and plugin factory move unchanged
into kwritedmodule.cpp, compiled only for the KDED module; kwrited.cpp is
what both builds share. Both builds produce the same code as before.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 655c52b..c32ca6f 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@ if (BUILD_AS_EXECUTABLE)
     install(FILES kwrited-autostart.desktop DESTINATION ${KDE_INSTALL_AUTOSTARTDIR})
 else ()
     kcoreaddons_add_plugin(kded_kwrited
-        SOURCES kwrited.cpp
+        SOURCES kwrited.cpp kwritedmodule.cpp
         INSTALL_NAMESPACE "kf6/kded"
     )
     set_target_properties(kded_kwrited PROPERTIES OUTPUT_NAME kwrited)
